@sentenz218 The regime certainly overstepped and made mistakes. But why did the author include this information about Kazakhstan in the video? Where, then, is the account of the gen0cide perpetrated by Europeans against the peoples of the USSR? About the invasion of the Mongols and Turks, if we really want to remember everything. About the victims of the famine among Russians, since it raged far beyond Kazakhstan? If you don't want to talk about Russia, what about Libya? Or other African countries?

In Russia, under any regime, life was worst for Russians. The "enslaved" peoples, unlike the Russians, were exempted from military service, serfdom, and some taxes. They completely retained local authority, which Moscow/St. Petersburg could neither remove nor appoint. Moreover, they enjoyed privileges unavailable to Russians; for instance, they had free access to natural resources, including hunting and fishing grounds.

By the way, you are insulting the peoples of the USSR. Some of them asked to join Russia or the USSR themselves to escape other neighbors. Some were sold by their previous owners. Some simply didn't care. Kazakhstan, for instance, made decisions on the matter several times. And Mongolia asked to join the USSR. The USSR was not just Russia. Stalin was a Georgian. Just as many Communist Party members were Ukrainians, Kazakhs, and so on. But the Russians are to blame for everything. Even the Communists fought against Great-Russian chauvinism. And the rest are slaves.

